Flex's scene and body network (moge-segment.safetensors): a small head that runs on the
features of MoGe-2 ViT-S (Ruicheng/moge-2-vits-normal, MIT, downloaded separately; not included
here), and tells each pixel apart as other, person, wall, sky, ground, ceiling, water, plant,
window, vehicle, animal, building or furniture; for a person's pixels, skin, hair or clothes,
and head, torso, arm, hand, leg or foot; and which person each belongs to. Trained for Flex by
crates/flex-depth/tools/moge/segment/run.py, with MoGe-2 frozen, on the pictures and labels of
COCO panoptic and DensePose-COCO (cocodataset.org), ADE20K's Scene Parsing set
(ade20k.csail.mit.edu), ATR (human parsing), CIHP (crowds of people, with their parts),
Danbooru-Parsing (anime portraits) and skytnt's anime-segmentation, none of which are included.
